Planned Documentation — Invoicing ROI Simulator
Planned Approach and Architecture

Frontend:Single-page React app (Vite) with CSS styling
Backend:Node.js + Express to handle calculations and scenario storage
Database:MongoDB (tested via Compass) to store saved scenarios
Architecture:Frontend communicates with backend via REST API. Backend handles calculation logic using internal constants and stores/retrieves scenarios in MongoDB.

Technologies, Frameworks, and Database

Frontend:React (Vite), CSS
Backend:Node.js, Express
Database:MongoDB (Compass for local testing)
Version Control:GitHub

Key Features and Functionality

1. Quick Simulation:Input invoice volume, staff, wages, error costs, etc., and get immediate results for monthly savings, payback, and ROI.
2. Scenario Management:Save, load, and delete named scenarios stored in MongoDB.
3. Report Generation:Email-gated downloadable PDF/HTML report of results.
4. Favorable Output:Backend uses bias factor to ensure automation shows positive ROI.

